{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1209236-what-are-your-favourite-dragonblood-charms","id":1209236,"title":"What are your favourite Dragonblood charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-20T07:27:50-07:00","id":1209236,"title":"What are your favourite Dragonblood charms?","content":"And why? <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">/10char</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:27:19-07:00","id":1209265,"title":"","content":"Oh jeez, how does one choose?<br /> <br /> \u200bFor a start, I like Warrant of Divine Safety; it's evocative of its Ability in a unique manner, has a potential for some very fun elemental displays, and I find it to have a particularly nice sense of how being Dragon Blooded entails a kind of natural command of elements, how the air leaps to serving your needs in that instance. On a practical level, it also feels like a very strong story enabler.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll probably come back later to relate some of my favourites in <i>all</i> of the Abilities, or at least most of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:32:03-07:00","id":1209268,"title":"","content":"I will be unoriginal and go with the Elemental Bolt up to Dragon Vortex attack. Why? Because I love awesome displays of raw elemental power of course.<br /> <br /> The Air War Signature charm is something that is very close to my heart but the whole War tree has made me want to play a young DB officer for sure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:51:39-07:00","id":1209275,"title":"","content":"Eternal Death-Banishing Blossom. It almost makes up for the grievous lack of a Senbonzakura-alike among the Artifacts published thus far. <i>Almost.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T09:07:26-07:00","id":1209278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1209236-what-are-your-favourite-dragonblood-charms?p=1209275#post1209275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It almost makes up for the grievous lack of a Senbonzakura-alike among the Artifacts published thus far.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI understand that the word means thousand cherry blossoms, but the reference to Artifacts specifically suggests to me that it's a reference I'm not getting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T09:24:11-07:00","id":1209283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1209236-what-are-your-favourite-dragonblood-charms?p=1209278#post1209278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI understand that the word means thousand cherry blossoms, but the reference to Artifacts specifically suggests to me that it's a reference I'm not getting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bleach. Senbonzakura is the sword of one of the characters, and when its Special Power is activated the blade turns into a storm of what looks like cherry petals but are actually a storm of swirling shrapnel under the user's control.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have much else going for it, but Bleach does have neat weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T09:51:40-07:00","id":1209296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1209236-what-are-your-favourite-dragonblood-charms?p=1209283#post1209283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't have much else going for it, but Bleach does have neat weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Soul Society arc is the <i>essence </i>of shonen battle anime. It also has a much more appealing artstyle than the others of the Big Three. That said, everything else about the series is indeed hot garbage (and JoJo's Battle Tendency arc does &quot;snappy encapsulation of an entire subgenre&quot; in an even more compact, 13 episode format).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T10:49:36-07:00","id":1209324,"title":"","content":"I think my favorite DB charms so far are Arbor Sentinel Technique and Exploding Evidence. Tree turret bow and &quot;They can't incriminate me if everything is on fire&quot; are just so much fun to me, I can't help but love them.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of really cool goodies in the charmset as a whole though. Truth-In-Stone Binding and Anathema-Sealing Tomb are also amazing, and Unmoving Center Enlightenment is a great concept, for instance. There's more but these are some of those that immediately come to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T10:54:15-07:00","id":1209326,"title":"","content":"I do love how many Fire-aligned charms give you different ways to immolate someone.<br /> <br /> Essence bolt? You're on fire.<br /> <br /> Explosive Dodge, and you're on fire.<br /> <br /> Did you try to cheat me in a game of cards? <b>Burn for it!</b><br /> <br /> Huh, this pie tastes like poison. And it has just burst into flame. Guess it was poison after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T11:15:35-07:00","id":1209331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1209236-what-are-your-favourite-dragonblood-charms?p=1209326#post1209326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do love how many Fire-aligned charms give you different ways to immolate someone.<br /> <br /> Essence bolt? You're on fire.<br /> <br /> Explosive Dodge, and you're on fire.<br /> <br /> Did you try to cheat me in a game of cards? <b>Burn for it!</b><br /> <br /> Huh, this pie tastes like poison. And it has just burst into flame. Guess it was poison after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>JJBA-A Abdul: \u201cI have learned that the only way to deal with this problem: Is to BURN IT.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T11:41:28-07:00","id":1209337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1209236-what-are-your-favourite-dragonblood-charms?p=1209326#post1209326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do love how many Fire-aligned charms give you different ways to immolate someone.<br /> <br /> Essence bolt? You're on fire.<br /> <br /> Explosive Dodge, and you're on fire.<br /> <br /> Did you try to cheat me in a game of cards? <b>Burn for it!</b><br /> <br /> Huh, this pie tastes like poison. And it has just burst into flame. Guess it was poison after all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For decades, we've known in RPGs that if a problem wasn't solved with judicious amounts of fire, it just means you haven't used enough fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T12:15:50-07:00","id":1209346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1209236-what-are-your-favourite-dragonblood-charms?p=1209337#post1209337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For decades, we've known in RPGs that if a problem wasn't solved with judicious amounts of fire, it just means you haven't used enough fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Burning Name sorcerer:<br /> Defining Intimacy: Sorcery can solve everything<br /> Major Intimacy: Fire can solve <i>most</i> things<br /> <br /> I have not yet gained a point of limit from countering either of these Intimacies, and my GM has tried hard (at my challenge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T13:14:42-07:00","id":1209368,"title":"","content":"<b>Safety Among Enemies</b> has always been one of my favorites - it's a great way for someone who's primarily a non-combatant to occasionally pull off a really, really useful move in a fight.<br /> <b>Wind-Carried Words Technique</b> is <i>just so useful.</i> Ditto for <b>Revelation-of-Associates Hunch</b>.<br /> I like <b>Intoxicating Lotus Manuscript</b> for the image of George R.R. Martin as a Dragon-Blooded, and <b>Seven Seas Wind-Luring Chanty</b> for the image of a bunch of sailors singing and a storm spirit singing along.<br /> <b>Fortune-from-Flotsam Ingenuity</b>. It may stray into the cartoonish, but that's part of why I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T13:29:36-07:00","id":1209373,"title":"","content":"I love how the essence 1 linguistics charm cryptic essence cypher gives characters an opportunity to lay the groundwork for a secret communications network by instilling intimacies.<br /> <br /> On the fire subject, there is a 5th edition Ars Magica book that has an NPC I wrote who has spent his entire life devising ways to be able to solve <u>any</u> problem with fire, and he may be the most fun thing that I've ever written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T14:14:48-07:00","id":1209396,"title":"","content":"One Forest, Many Trees for sure. Really cool charm concept for a character archetype that doesn't get much mechanical support otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:04:31-07:00","id":1209437,"title":"","content":"I love almost all of Linguistics, but if I had to choose just <i>one</i> Charm, I think it's gotta be Seething Firebreak Technique from Bureaucracy. Exposing conspirators against you by <i>encouraging them</i> is just lovely. Let your enemies immolate themselves (socially)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T17:11:09-07:00","id":1209825,"title":"","content":"The performance charm that lets you make a fight look staged to bystanders. So many clever rapscallion hijinks to be had with that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24157-pangudelegate","name":"PanguDelegate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T06:04:31-07:00","id":1209994,"title":"","content":"I can't help but love the Ride charm that lets you stampede an entire army.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T06:04:18-07:00","id":1210380,"title":"",